1
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:12,780
A robot vacuum cleaner walks around the edge of a room shaped like a regular hexagon.

2
00:00:12,830 --> 00:00:17,290
It turns at each corner, until it faces the way it started.

3
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:20,380
How far has it turned altogether, in degrees?

4
00:00:20,430 --> 00:00:23,970
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:29,200
It ends up facing the same way, so it has turned through one full turn.

6
00:00:29,250 --> 00:00:31,220
That is 360 degrees.

7
00:00:31,270 --> 00:00:36,320
Remember: angles on a straight line add up to 180 degrees.

8
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:38,580
Extend one side at each corner.

9
00:00:38,630 --> 00:00:43,090
The exterior angle is between the extension and the next side.

10
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:47,650
The interior and exterior angles add up to 180 degrees.

11
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:52,780
Walking all the way round any polygon, you turn through one full turn.

12
00:00:52,830 --> 00:00:57,730
So the exterior angles of any polygon add up to 360 degrees.

13
00:00:57,780 --> 00:00:58,420
Your turn.

14
00:00:58,470 --> 00:01:03,030
How much does the robot turn at each corner of the regular hexagon?

15
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:06,280
Pause the video and try it.

16
00:01:06,330 --> 00:01:10,790
360 shared between 6 equal corners is 60 degrees each.

17
00:01:10,840 --> 00:01:16,510
In a regular polygon, each exterior angle is 360 divided by N.

18
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:21,660
So the number of sides is 360 divided by the exterior angle.

19
00:01:21,710 --> 00:01:23,140
Here is the method.

20
00:01:23,190 --> 00:01:28,290
Step 1: remember the exterior angles add up to 360 degrees.

21
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:33,540
Step 2: in a regular polygon, each one is 360 divided by N.

22
00:01:33,590 --> 00:01:38,930
Step 3: the interior angle is 180 minus the exterior angle.

23
00:01:38,980 --> 00:01:43,660
Step 4: to find N, divide 360 by the exterior angle.

24
00:01:43,710 --> 00:01:48,380
A regular polygon has exterior angles of 24 degrees.

25
00:01:48,430 --> 00:01:50,560
360 divided by 24 is 15.

26
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:52,560
It has 15 sides.

27
00:01:52,610 --> 00:01:53,260
Your turn.

28
00:01:53,310 --> 00:01:57,220
What is the exterior angle of a regular 9-sided polygon?

29
00:01:57,270 --> 00:02:00,180
Pause and work it out.

30
00:02:00,230 --> 00:02:04,050
360 divided by 9 is 40 degrees.

31
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:08,750
Find the interior angle of a regular 20-sided polygon.

32
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:13,360
The exterior angle is 360 divided by 20, which is 18.

33
00:02:13,410 --> 00:02:18,870
The interior angle is 180 minus 18, which is 162 degrees.

34
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:23,520
Can a regular polygon have exterior angles of 50 degrees?

35
00:02:23,570 --> 00:02:25,560
360 divided by 50 is 7.2.

36
00:02:25,610 --> 00:02:28,890
That is not a whole number, so no.

37
00:02:28,940 --> 00:02:32,230
Nina finds the exterior angle sum of an octagon.

38
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:34,170
Which line is wrong?

39
00:02:34,220 --> 00:02:35,290
Line 1 is wrong.

40
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:38,000
That is the interior angle sum.

41
00:02:38,050 --> 00:02:43,180
The exterior angles of every polygon add up to 360 degrees.

42
00:02:43,230 --> 00:02:47,270
Programmers draw regular polygons with turtle graphics.

43
00:02:47,320 --> 00:02:52,970
Move forward, then turn 360 divided by N degrees, and repeat N times.

44
00:02:53,020 --> 00:02:54,260
One last question.

45
00:02:54,310 --> 00:02:58,000
A regular polygon has exterior angles of 45 degrees.

46
00:02:58,050 --> 00:03:00,010
What is each interior angle?

47
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:03,350
Pause the video and answer.

48
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:06,120
180 minus 45 is 135 degrees.

49
00:03:06,170 --> 00:03:09,040
It is a regular octagon.

50
00:03:09,090 --> 00:03:15,030
To remember: the exterior angles of any polygon add up to 360 degrees.

51
00:03:15,080 --> 00:03:18,480
Regular: each is 360 divided by N.

52
00:03:18,530 --> 00:03:22,270
Interior plus exterior is 180 degrees.

53
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:26,050
N is 360 divided by the exterior angle.

54
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:31,230
Great work! Now practise lesson 5.3 on Camday.
